{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{artist: Mary Byrne / Eleanor Hull (trans.) / Traditional Irish}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 3/4}
{score: be-thou-my-vision.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Vision, O [D]Lord of my [Bm]heart
[D]Naught be all [G]else to me, [D]save that Thou [A]art
[D]Thou my best [G]Thought, by [D]day or by [Bm]night
[G]Waking or [D]sleeping, Thy [A]presence my [D]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Wisdom, and [D]Thou my true [Bm]Word
[D]I ever with [G]Thee and Thou [D]with me, [A]Lord
[D]Thou my great [G]Father, I [D]Thy true [Bm]son
[G]Thou in me [D]dwelling, and [A]I with Thee [D]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Be Thou my battle [G]Shield, sword for the [D]fight
[D]Be Thou my [G]Dignity, [D]Thou my de[A]light
[D]Thou my soul's [G]Shelter, [D]Thou my high [Bm]Tower
[G]Raise Thou me [D]heavenward, [A]O Power of my [D]power
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Riches I [G]heed not, nor [D]man's empty [Bm]praise
[D]Thou mine In[G]heritance, [D]now and al[A]ways
[D]Thou and Thou [G]only, [D]first in my [Bm]heart
[G]High King of [D]Heaven, my [A]Treasure Thou [D]art
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]High King of [G]Heaven, my [D]victory [Bm]won
[D]May I reach [G]Heaven's joys, O [D]bright Heaven's [A]Sun
[D]Heart of my [G]own heart, what[D]ever be[Bm]fall
[G]Still be my [D]Vision, O [A]Ruler of [D]all
{end_of_verse}
